{"id":2046,"level":79,"name":"Виграш пішака (1)","group":"Практика","format":27,"description":"<p><span style='font-weight: 400;'>As chess players get stronger, they need a lower material advantage to win. In the beginning, it is difficult to mate with a king and queen against a bare king. As soon as chess players get better, they also succeed in checkmating with only a king and rook.&nbsp;</span></p>  <p></p>  <p><span style='font-weight: 400;'>If you follow games of the world's best players, you will regularly see that winning just a single pawn can be sufficient for victory. Every piece of wood on the board is important!&nbsp;</span></p>  <p></p>  <p><span style='font-weight: 400;'>So in this lesson we won't be looking for great combinations that win huge amounts of material. The goal is more modest: win a pawn.</span></p>  <p></p>  <p><b>What do you have to do?</b></p>  <p><span style='font-weight: 400;'>Look for a vulnerable enemy pawn and try to win it. Sometimes you will need a trick to pull this off.</span></p>","assignment":"","stickerID":0,"examples":[{"fen":"rnbqk2r/pp2nppp/3b4/2p5/4Pp2/1N3N2/PPPP2PP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 8","pgn":"{[%evp 0,3,93,102,91,85]} 8. e5 Bc7 9. Nxc5 * ","text":"<p>пішак на c5 захищається лише один раз. Вигнавши слона за допомогою <strong>1.e5!</strong> білі можуть виграти пішака на c5.</p>","format":27},{"fen":"1q1rr1k1/pp1b1ppp/5n2/2Pp2B1/3Pp3/2N3P1/PP3P1P/R2RQ1K1 w - - 0 19","pgn":"{[%evp 0,3,190,177,183,180]} 19. Bxf6 gxf6 20. Nxd5 * ","text":"<p>Цього разу мішенню є центральний пішак на d5. Білі знову ліквідовують захисника за допомогою <strong>1.Bxf6! gxf6 2.Nxd5 </strong>Білі не лише виграли пішака, але й послабили структуру чорних.</p>","format":27},{"fen":"r1b2rk1/1p1n1pp1/p2p3p/2pP2n1/P1P1PN2/1P1B2NP/6P1/2R2RK1 w - - 0 19","pgn":"{[%evp 0,3,125,125,123,123]} 19. Nf5 {[%csl Rd6,Gf5][%cal Gf5d6]} Ne5 20. Nxd6 {[%csl Gd6]} * ","text":"","format":27}],"puzzles":[{"id":77151,"fen":"3qr3/1p4kp/p2r1pp1/3P4/1P1Q4/P4P1P/8/3RR1K1 b 